export const SUPPORTED_PRINTERS_TEXT = "ID CARD PRINTING SOFTWARE FREE - SUPPORTED PRINTERS\nCopyright (c) 2026 Josh McNabb. All rights reserved.\n\nCards are printed through the printer's own Windows driver, so the\nprinter's driver must be installed first. Each card template has its card\nsize: CR80 (85.6 x 54 mm, the usual ID card), CR79 (83.9 x 52.1 mm), CR100\n(98.5 x 67 mm) or a custom size, and the printer must accept that size. Cards\nare sent at the printer's own resolution: 600 dpi for 600 dpi printers,\notherwise 300 dpi. How much the software can report about the printer depends\non its driver.\n\n\nHID FARGO PRINTERS\nPrinting, live status and alerts on every model. Ribbon and film levels, the\ncard counter and flipper (dual-sided) detection are read from the FARGO\ndriver and shown when the driver reports them; film levels only apply to\nretransfer (HDP) models. The software was developed against the HDP5000 and\nchecked on Windows 11; the other models use the same FARGO driver family but\nhave not all been tested with this software.\n\n  HID FARGO HDP5000                    Retransfer (HDP)\n  HID FARGO HDP5600                    Retransfer (HDP)\n  HID FARGO HDP6600                    Retransfer (HDP)\n  HID FARGO HDP8500                    Industrial retransfer (HDP)\n  HID FARGO DTC1250e                   Direct-to-card\n  HID FARGO DTC1500                    Direct-to-card\n  HID FARGO DTC4250e                   Direct-to-card\n  HID FARGO DTC4500e                   Direct-to-card\n  HID FARGO DTC5500LMX                 Direct-to-card, high volume\n  HID FARGO C50                        Direct-to-card\n  HID FARGO DTC1000Me                  Direct-to-card, mobile\n  HID FARGO INK1000                    Inkjet card printer\n\n\nBASIC SUPPORT - OTHER CARD PRINTERS\nAny card printer with a Windows driver for the card size used, for example\nZebra, Evolis, Magicard, Entrust (Datacard) and IDP printers. Printing works\nthrough the driver, and alerts are limited to what Windows reports (offline,\npaper/card out, jams, errors). Ribbon levels are not shown.\n\n\nDUAL-SIDED PRINTING\nPrinters with a flipper module print both sides in one pass. Printers\nwithout one can still make dual-sided cards: print all the fronts, flip the\nstack, then press \"Print backs\" in the print queue (Settings > Printing >\nHow the back is printed > Manually).\n\n\nNOT SUPPORTED\nOrdinary office and photo printers, label printers, and network print\nservices that do not use a Windows card-printer driver.\n\nPrinter names and trade marks belong to their owners. Their mention here does\nnot mean they endorse this software. Support is provided \"as is\" and without\nwarranty, as set out in LICENSE.txt.\n";
